plore teachers\' thoughts and experiences in more depth. They can provide detailed insights into how teachers perceive using…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s great that you\'re confident about using semi-structured interviews. Let\'s think about why interviews might be more suitable than other methods like surveys or observations. What specific as…\nUSER: I think semi-structured interviews are a good fit because they allow me to explore teachers\' thoughts and experiences in more depth. They can provide detailed insights into how teachers perceive using…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s clear that you believe semi-structured interviews are a good fit because they allow you to explore teachers\' thoughts and experiences in depth. Can you think about what specific aspects of …\nUSER: I think semi-structured interviews are a good fit because they allow me to explore teachers\' thoughts and experiences in more depth. They can provide detailed insights into how teachers perceive using…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s excellent that you\'re confident in using semi-structured interviews because they allow you to explore teachers\' thoughts and experiences in depth. Can you elaborate on how interviews can ca…\nUSER: Semi-structured interviews seem to be the right choice because they allow me to delve into the personal and contextual factors influencing teachers\' use of digital tools. They can capture the nuances …\nASSISTANT: Mary, it sounds like you\'re feeling more confident that semi-structured interviews are the right choice for your research. Interviews can indeed capture the nuances of teachers\' experiences and percep…\nUSER: Semi-structured interviews seem to be the right choice because they allow me to delve into the personal and contextual factors influencing teachers\' use of digital tools. They can capture the nuances …\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s great to hear that you\'re feeling more confident about using semi-structured interviews. Let\'s now consider some alternative methods to broaden your perspective. Here are three plausible al…\nUSER: I see how each of these alternative methods could provide valuable data, but they might not capture the same depth and nuance as semi-structured interviews. For example, a survey would be good for get…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s excellent that you\'re considering how each method aligns with your research question. Let\'s summarize your reflections:\n\n1. **Online Survey of Teachers**:\n   - **Pros**: Can gather data fro…\nUSER: I see how each method has its pros and cons, but semi-structured interviews seem to be the best fit for capturing the depth and nuance of teachers\' perceptions of digital tools. Surveys might miss the…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s great to hear that you\'re feeling more confident about your choice of semi-structured interviews. Reflecting on the alternatives has clearly shown that interviews align well with your resea…\nUSER: I see how each method has its pros and cons, but semi-structured interviews seem to be the best fit for capturing the depth and nuance of teachers\' perceptions of digital tools. Surveys might miss the…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s fantastic to see that you\'ve solidified your choice of semi-structured interviews and feel more confident about it. You\'ve done a great job of considering the strengths and limitations of e…\nUSER: I see how each method has its pros and cons, but semi-structured interviews seem to be the best fit for capturing the depth and nuance of teachers\' perceptions of digital tools. Surveys might miss the…\nASSISTANT: Mary, it\'s fantastic to see that you\'ve solidified your choice of semi-structured interviews and feel more confident about it. You\'ve done a great job of considering the strengths and limitations of e…\nUSER: I feel much more confident that semi-structured interviews are the best fit for my research question. They align well with my goal of understanding the depth and nuance of teachers\' perceptions of dig…\n\nSurvey:\nQ1: How well did the